 == 0 or c == 0:\n                    result[r][c] = 2\n                else:\n                    result[r][c] = 1\n    return result\n```\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-ac2ef703\nTest input (20x26):\n8 7 7 7 8 7 8 7 7 7 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 7 7\n8 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 7 8\n7 8 8 8 7 7 8 7 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 8\n7 8 7 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 8 7 7 8\n8 7 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7\n8 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 7 8 8 8 7\n8 8 8 8 7 7 8 7 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 8 7 8 7 7 8 8\n7 7 7 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 7 8\n8 8 8 7 7 7 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 7 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 7 8\n8 8 8 8 8 7 8 7 7 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 8 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 8\n8 8 7 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 7 8 7 7 8 8 8 7\n8 8 7 8 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 7\n8 8 8 8 8 7 8 7 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 8\n7 7 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 7 7 7 8 8 7 8 7 8\n8 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 8 7 7 7 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 7 8\n7 8 8 7 7 8 7 7 8 8 7 8 8 7 8 7 8 8 7 7 8 7 8 8 8 8\n7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 7 8\n7 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 8 7 7 8 8 7 7\n7 8 7 7 8 7 7 7 7 8 7 7 8 8 7 8 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 8 8 7\n8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 8 7 7 8 7 7 8 8 8 8 8 7 7 8\nWrong attempts used: 1/8. Demo requests used: 0/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"The task is to transform a grid based on the properties of its foreground connected components. Based on the analysis of the demonstration pairs, the transformation rule is as follows:\n\n1.  Identify the background color ($bg$) as the most frequent color in the grid.\n2.  Identify the foreground pixels as those with a color different from $bg$.\n3.  For each connected component of foreground pixels (using 4-connectivity):\n    *   Determine its size (number of pixels in the component).\n    *   Map the size to a new color based on the remainder of the size modulo 3:\n        *   If $size \\pmod 3 == 1$, the new color is 1.\n        *   If $size \\pmod 3 == 2$, the new color is 3.\n        *   If $size \\pmod 3 == 0$, the new color is 2.\n4.  Background pixels retain their original color.\n\nThis rule `size % 3 == 1 -> 1`, `size % 3 == 2 -> 3`, `size % 3 == 0 -> 2` is consistent with observations from all provided demonstration pairs (e.g., size 4 maps to 1, size 3 maps to 2, size 2 maps to 3).\n\nThe provided code implements this logic using BFS to find connected components and updates the grid accordingly.\n\n```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return grid\n    \n    from collections import Counter\n    cells = [cell for row in grid for cell in row]\n    counts = Counter(cells)\n    bg_val = counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n    \n    height = len(grid)\n    width = len(grid[0])\n    visited = [[False] * width for _ in range(height)]\n    res = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    for r in range(height):\n        for c in range(width):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val != bg_val and not visited[r][c]:\n                # BFS to find component\n                component = []\n                stack = [(r, c)]\n                visited[r][c] = True\n                component.append((r, c))\n                \n                idx = 0\n                while idx < len(stack):\n                    curr_r, curr_c = stack[idx]\n                    idx += 1\n                    for dr, dc in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n                        nr, nc = curr_r + dr, curr_c + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < height and 0 <= nc < width:\n                            if not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] != bg_val:\n                                visited[nr][nc] = True\n                                stack.append((nr, nc))\n                                component.append((nr, nc))\n                \n                size = len(component)\n                rem = size % 3\n                \n                # Mapping derived from pairs:\n                # size % 3 == 1 -> 1\n                # size % 3 == 2 -> 3\n                # size % 3 == 0 -> 2\n                if rem == 1:\n                    color = 1\n                elif rem == 2:\n                    color = 3\n                else: # rem == 0\n                    color = 2\n                \n                for rr, cc in component:\n                    res[rr][cc] = color\n                    \n    return res\n```\n\n```json\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}\n```","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":true}}]}